# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SHIVA environment
#
# Phase 1 (the spatial OS shell) needs NONE of these — it runs with an empty
# .env.local. Everything below is scaffolding for Phase 2+, documented here so
# the config layer doesn't have to be re-plumbed later.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in as you enable each capability.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Phase 2: AI brain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google AI Studio key. Server-side only — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, or it
# ships to the browser and becomes a public key.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Leave as the alias unless you have a reason not to: it tracks the current
# flash model. A pinned version silently 404s once Google retires it, and the
# error reads like a bad key rather than a stale model name.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest

# Voice. SHIVA speaks with Gemini's neural TTS and falls back to the browser's
# built-in synthesis if the request fails or the key is absent — the browser is
# the *fast* path, so speech still happens rather than not happening.
# Voices: Kore (level), Puck (warm), Charon (deep), Aoede, Fenrir.
GEMINI_TTS_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts
GEMINI_TTS_VOICE=Kore

# ── Live voice agent (Deepgram) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables the "Live" button: one websocket carrying microphone audio up and
# agent audio down, so you can interrupt it mid-sentence. Without this key the
# Live button is disabled and the wake-word path still works.
#
# Server-side only, and unusually strictly so: a browser cannot set headers on a
# WebSocket, so the credential travels in the subprotocol where any script on
# the page can read it. The server mints 30-second tokens instead
# (app/api/voice/token). Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# https://console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# ── Phase 3: Google Calendar + Gmail ─────────────────────────────────────────
# OAuth 2.0 Web Application client from https://console.cloud.google.com
# Authorised redirect URI: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback

# ── Phase 3: coding companion (Projects panel) ───────────────────────────────
# Fine-grained PAT, read-only: `contents`, `pull_requests`, `checks`.
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Phase 1: telemetry (all optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Weather uses Open-Meteo, which needs no key. Set a fallback location for when
# the browser denies geolocation. Defaults to 0,0 if unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LAT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LON=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LOCATION_LABEL=
